{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../agent-source/rawnode.go | sed -n '532,551p'; sed -n '30,75p' ../agent-source/logger.go; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('../direct-checks/563626623cf144f5a145827eb45c0351/plan.json'));print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in p.items() if k\"'!='\"'harness'},indent=2)); print('PREREQ',p['harness']['prerequisites'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"   532\t\n   533\t// ReportUnreachable reports the given node is not reachable for the last send.\n   534\tfunc (rn *RawNode) ReportUnreachable(id uint64) {\n   535\t\t_ = rn.raft.Step(pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgUnreachable, From: id})\n   536\t}\n   537\t\n   538\t// ReportSnapshot reports the status of the sent snapshot.\n   539\tfunc (rn *RawNode) ReportSnapshot(id uint64, status SnapshotStatus) {\n   540\t\trej := status == SnapshotFailure\n   541\t\n   542\t\t_ = rn.raft.Step(pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgSnapStatus, From: id, Reject: rej})\n   543\t}\n   544\t\n   545\t// TransferLeader tries to transfer leadership to the given transferee.\n   546\tfunc (rn *RawNode) TransferLeader(transferee uint64) {\n   547\t\t_ = rn.raft.Step(pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgTransferLeader, From: transferee})\n   548\t}\n   549\t\n   550\t// ForgetLeader forgets a follower's current leader, changing it to None.\n   551\t// See (Node).ForgetLeader for details.\n\tErrorf(format string, v ...interface{})\n\n\tInfo(v ...interface{})\n\tInfof(format string, v ...interface{})\n\n\tWarning(v ...interface{})\n\tWarningf(format string, v ...interface{})\n\n\tFatal(v ...interface{})\n\tFatalf(format string, v ...interface{})\n\n\tPanic(v ...interface{})\n\tPanicf(format string, v ...interface{})\n}\n\nfunc SetLogger(l Logger) {\n\traftLoggerMu.Lock()\n\traftLogger = l\n\traftLoggerMu.Unlock()\n}\n\nfunc ResetDefaultLogger() {\n\tSetLogger(defaultLogger)\n}\n\nfunc getLogger() Logger {\n\traftLoggerMu.Lock()\n\tdefer raftLoggerMu.Unlock()\n\treturn raftLogger\n}\n\nvar (\n\tdefaultLogger = &DefaultLogger{Logger: log.New(os.Stderr, \"raft\", log.LstdFlags)}\n\tdiscardLogger = &DefaultLogger{Logger: log.New(io.Discard, \"\", 0)}\n\traftLoggerMu  sync.Mutex\n\traftLogger    = Logger(defaultLogger)\n)\n\nconst (\n\tcalldepth = 2\n)\n\n// DefaultLogger is a default implementation of the Logger interface.\ntype DefaultLogger struct {\n\t*log.Logger\n\tdebug bool\n{\n  \"description\": \"Fresh direct check of C-auto-leave-continuation, based on the explored real-node history. Start transfer between joint configuration application and its Advance; after bounded TimeoutNow loss and timeout, compare complete behavioral projections at the same phase of two successive ten-tick heartbeat cycles. Retain both projections and raw counters. Later unrelated proposal is a distinct rescue diagnostic.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"C-auto-leave-continuation\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"BD-auto-leave\",\n    \"BD-transfer-expiry\",\n    \"BD-advance\"\n  ],\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MON-idle-cycle\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"CK-no-idle-cycle\",\n      \"event\": \"cycle_result\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"BD-auto-leave\",\n        \"BD-transfer-expiry\",\n        \"BD-advance\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"M-auto\",\n          \"M-conf-contract\",\n          \"M-auto-contract\",\n          \"M-election\",\n          \"M-transfer-abort\",\n          \"M-apply-response\",\n          \"M-advance\",\n          \"M-state-fields\",\n          \"M-memory-fields\",\n          \"M-random\",\n          \"M-progress-fields\",\n          \"M-inflight-fields\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"BD-auto-leave\",\n          \"BD-transfer-expiry\",\n          \"BD-advance\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"Correlate result to one admitted configuration operation using operation_id; config_index is retained in the prerequisite and result and represents the observed committed entering record. The predicate excludes a fair closed idle cycle, not absence before a made-up deadline. State equality and the source of the periodic transition establish repeatability; no unrelated operation completion is assumed.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Only declared failed_transfer_idle scenario; rescue output is diagnostic.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [\n          \"Correspondence review of exact projection and periodic suffix is required.\"\n        ],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"A nonrepeating endpoint is not by itself a positive liveness proof.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"scenario\",\n          \"op\": \"eq\",\n          \"value\": \"failed_transfer_idle\",\n          \"reference\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admitted\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"CK-no-idle-cycle\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_assertion\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"event\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"cycle_result\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"forbidden_idle_cycle\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": false,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": null,\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"operation_id\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"No fully observed closed, drained, role-stable heartbeat/tick cycle may leave the admitted automatic exit pending after transfer clears. forbidden_idle_cycle is computed from exact structural equality of two live-state projections, drained queues/Ready work, only-heartbeat traffic, stable roles, no new application batches, pending AutoLeave and unchanged applied/committed/log tail. Failure is a finite cycle witness with source-based repeatability; false only means this specific witness was not found, not universal eventual completion.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"The reflection observer intentionally excludes logger, unlocked mutex and call-count diagnostics; review must verify these are behaviorally inert for the captured serialized suffix.\",\n    \"Entropy is not compared globally; the observed stable-role heartbeat-only suffix must be shown not to consume election randomness.\",\n    \"This property finds a closed counterexample cycle; a false result would not prove the general eventual-progress obligation.\"\n  ]\n}\nPREREQ [{'alias': 'admitted', 'event': 'admitted', 'conditions': [{'field': 'scenario', 'op': 'eq', 'value': 'failed_transfer_idle', 'reference': None}, {'field': 'triggered', 'op': 'eq', 'value': True, 'reference': None}, {'field': 'transferee', 'op': 'eq', 'value': 2, 'reference': None}, {'field': 'dropped_timeout_now', 'op': 'eq', 'value': 1, 'reference': None}, {'field': 'role', 'op': 'eq', 'value': 'StateLeader', 'reference': None}, {'field': 'drained', 'op': 'eq', 'value': True, 'reference': None}, {'field': 'all_applied_config', 'op': 'eq', 'value': True, 'reference': None}, {'field': 'config.auto_leave', 'op': 'eq', 'value': True, 'reference': None}]}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The runner reproduced the cycle, and the raw snapshots compare equal. All three nodes had applied index 5, no storage work or callbacks remained queued, and transfer had cleared. The interval completed 40 heartbeat messages and 30 Ready batches without creating an exit entry.\n\nSource tracing supports repeatability here: heartbeats reset follower election timers, the leader retains quorum, and no application acknowledgment is generated to retry the rejected proposal. The later client proposal successfully triggers exit; that is an additional stimulus, not autonomous continuation."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nartifact='44ecdde6ffdd41aab4fbf9cfe88f0cb8'; run='e30e751a96ef45c8b43640539253ffe4'; cid='c1ba7e9ff9034a728850b297376ecbb8'\nrationale='''Reviewed artifact 44ecdde6ffdd41aab4fbf9cfe88f0cb8 version 1 against its saved C-auto-leave-continuation version 1, fixed plan, fixed assurance_generated_test.go, and raw stdout/stderr for CheckRun e30e751a96ef45c8b43640539253ffe4. The process completed with exit 0; this is not the verdict. The independently declared failed_transfer_idle scenario has exactly one admission (event index 2) and one cycle result (index 5), correlated by the stable operation_id remove-node3-implicit-1. Both carry observed configuration index 5. The result compares forbidden_idle_cycle=true against required false; assessment parsing has no errors and prerequisites actually matched.\n\nResponsibility: raftpb/raft.proto 121-128 and 148-150 distinguish automatic joint exit from the explicit mode requiring a caller proposal. tracker.Config.AutoLeave likewise assigns this transition to Raft when possible. The entering operation is already committed, applied and acknowledged; the general permission to drop client proposals does not transfer this pending internal exit to the caller. raft.appliedTo 755-760 explicitly recognizes transfer-time rejection and promises a later advance retry. The claim requires an enabled automatic continuation under healthy idle operation, not exit within ten or thirty ticks. Available membership includes leader 1 and voter 2 in both sets; outgoing set {1,2,3} also remains fully live. There is no unavailable quorum or removed leader preventing the internal proposal.\n\nEntry and history: fixed harness lines 108-131 construct real RawNodes with CheckQuorum, bootstrap identical voters, fully process bootstrap, and elect node 1 via actual target-generated messages. No fabricated reply or direct raft-field assignment prepares leadership, commitment or application. Lines 44-80 call Ready, synchronously persist entries and HardState, decode and apply actual committed configuration records, queue the resulting Ready messages, and Advance. For the unique entering record, TransferLeader(2) interleaves AFTER ApplyConfChange and BEFORE Advance (66-80). RawNode is thread-unsafe, but calls here are serial, and neither Ready nor Advance forbids intervening serialized input. This preserves precisely the original overlap rather than draining it away. TransferLeader is the public wrapper over MsgTransferLeader. The only drop policy is TimeoutNow during a bounded prefix (92-93,138-140); exactly one such message was observed dropped. Actual peer traffic otherwise passes through FIFO delivery. The implementation allows network message loss; reliable local Ready work is never dropped. MemoryStorage completion models successful durable IO in this crash-free scope. No snapshot is taken/restored, no restart occurs, and no discarded configuration is claimed as applied.\n\nObserved premises: stdout line 53 records entering joint configuration at term 2/index 5, transferee 2, commit 5 and applied 4, showing that application accounting has not yet acknowledged the entering record. Line 56 records all three nodes applied/committed through 5, AutoLeave=true, transfer active, exactly one dropped TimeoutNow and no queued work. Line 57 records transfer cleared at tick 10 while the same leader remains. The two full state events occupy stdout JSON lines 58-67 and 68-78 respectively: Go test chunks a large Output string across records, so I concatenated Output fragments in order before decoding the complete event lines. Both raw snapshot strings are equal; this is independently checkable from the retained bytes, not inferred from tests_passed. Cycle result records same_state, drained, only_heartbeats, roles_stable and unchanged_tail all true; 40 messages and 30 Ready batches completed, apply_delta=0, and AutoLeave/outgoing voters remain. The runner's event indices are 4 for cycle_start and 5 for cycle_result.\n\nObserver and repeatability: fixed harness 184-220 structurally reads every RawNode field and recursively its raft, log, actual MemoryStorage, voter configuration, Progress/Inflights (including private counters/buffers), pending messages/reads, unstable state, previous Ready state and stepsOnAdvance. It reads live values at serial drained boundaries, not a stale Status cache; all contents of log entries are retained, not just lengths or numeric positions. The observer omits only exact logger/trace fields, MemoryStorage callStats and its mutex. callStats only accumulates diagnostic method-call counts and is not used to branch in Storage; all mutex acquisitions finish before these serial reads. No concurrent writer exists. The default logger does not alter protocol state, tracing is disabled in this default no-tag build, and the fixed harness supplies no callback logger. Slice capacities and pointer allocation identities are omitted: in this suffix log/config contents are not mutated, no new entry/worker is admitted, and message buffer allocations cannot affect logical message values. Function code identities are retained; bound raft receivers remain the same allocated nodes throughout, and tick/step functions only change on authority transitions, absent here.\n\nThe snapshots contain electionElapsed=heartbeatElapsed=0 on all nodes, leader/follower roles 2/0/0, Term=2, leader=1, randomizedElectionTimeout values 17/15/19, no unstable work, empty internal/external queues, and no pending read or Advance callbacks. Storage HardState and complete logs are identical. Leader progress has Match=5, Next=6, StateReplicate and zero inflights for each voter. Each repeated tick gives the leader a heartbeat; each follower's tick raises its election timer only to one before delivered heartbeat resets it. Every tenth leader tick checks a live joint quorum and resets activity before replies restore it. Heartbeat replies neither append (peers are caught up and replicating) nor process read work (empty context). Thus the observed cycle does not call resetRandomizedElectionTimeout or consume external randomness; captured timeout values and source branch conditions suffice. Map visitation for heartbeat output is sorted. There is no asynchronous Node goroutine: the test uses RawNode only. The external policy for the continuation repeats Tick on nodes 1,2,3 then full Ready/message draining, with no further drops. Absolute diagnostic tick and message counters do not choose protocol inputs within this repeating policy. The test's later rescue is explicitly a separate phase; it is not part of the proposed infinite extension. These facts close the behavior-relevant state and schedule, so the observed finite cycle supplies a repeatable fair non-progress witness, not a time-based inference.\n\nCause and completed work: application acknowledgment calls appliedTo while leadTransferee=2; the generic proposal guard rejects the zero ConfChangeV2. Abort only clears leadTransferee. Heartbeat-only Ready lacks CommittedEntries, so acceptReady schedules no MsgStorageApplyResp and Advance has no application callback; no other read source path retries this pending exit in the idle suffix. All caller obligations required for the witness are completed at its endpoint (drained=true, applied=applying=committed=5, empty unstable and stepsOnAdvance on all nodes). There are no workers, network sockets, joins or shutdown callbacks to omit. RawNode has no Stop duty; cleanup does not manufacture the observation. Lines 173-175 then submit an unrelated ordinary proposal and complete its Ready work. Stdout line 83 records commit/applied/last=7 and final voters {1,2}, AutoLeave=false. This is contrary evidence to irreversible or unconditional stalling and corroborates the distinct later-application trigger, not autonomous completion.\n\nNo correspondence issue was found for this concrete violating cycle. It answers the candidate's idle failed-transfer continuation question; it does not establish a safety violation, a wall-clock deadline, or all possible configuration/transport histories. The fixed Boolean assertion is a sufficient counterexample detector. Its false value in another execution would only rule out that closed-cycle witness, not prove eventual completion. No weakened requirement or rerun of changed bytes is used in this review.'''\nsources=[dict(id='M-transfer-api',file='rawnode.go',start_line=545,end_line=548,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-trace-nop',file='state_trace_nop.go',start_line=15,end_line=50,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-default-logger',file='logger.go',start_line=44,end_line=75,kind='code_observation')]\nss=['M-conf-contract','M-auto-contract','M-auto','M-proposal','M-election','M-transfer-abort','M-transfer','M-transfer-api','M-api','M-raw-api','M-bootstrap','M-send','M-ready-contract','M-async-contract','M-apply-response','M-advance','M-support','M-follower-log','M-replicate','M-tracker','M-votes','M-state-fields','M-memory-fields','M-random','M-progress-fields','M-inflight-fields','M-trace-nop','M-default-logger']\nlimits=['Result applies to the fixed normal Ready/Advance, no-crash, retained-leader schedule; asynchronous storage and early-Advance orderings are separate variants.','No numeric deadline or consensus-safety violation is claimed. Repeatability is a source-supported finite cycle argument, not execution of infinite time.','Later unrelated proposals or successful leadership changes can restore automatic exit; availability impact depends on subsequent membership/failure history.','The reflection projection is sufficient for this inert heartbeat suffix; it is not claimed as a generic complete state abstraction for arbitrary concurrent or allocation-sensitive executions.']\nreview=dict(action='review',artifact_id=artifact,rationale='Complete current checker correspondence for the actual closed idle-cycle witness; no source or artifact inputs are changed.',sources=sources,review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ss,rationale=rationale,counterevidence=['A later unrelated proposal actually completed the exit at index 7 in the same run.','New leader election and application of its no-op can also trigger appliedTo; this run retained leadership.'],limitations=limits,report_title='领导权转移失败后自动退出联合配置缺少重试触发',report_answer='实际检查中，转移超时后节点仍停留在索引 5 的联合配置；随后 10 个 tick 完成 40 条心跳消息和 30 个 Ready 批次，完整行为状态再次相同，自动退出未获触发。另行提交普通提案后才推进至索引 7 并退出联合配置；该结果限于已核对的稳定领导者与空闲调度，不主张安全性破坏或固定时间期限。')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=[artifact,run,cid,'C-auto-leave-continuation','B-auto-leave','B-transfer','B-application','M-auto','M-advance'],answered='Fresh fixed CheckRun e30e751a96ef45c8b43640539253ffe4 completed normally and measured a violated no-closed-idle-cycle assertion. Current correspondence reconstructs the actual admission at event 2, full state snapshots at events 4/5, healthy periodic transport and completed caller work. The two state projections are equal with no unmodeled enabled continuation in this heartbeat suffix: transfer abort clears the blocker, but empty Ready/Advance supplies no appliedTo callback. A later ordinary proposal is retained as a separate successful rescue, excluding irreversible stalling.',remaining=['At the next related map handoff, replace the original automatic-retry unknown with the sourced conditional relationship and cite this assessment/review.','Independent frontier remains: early Advance versus configuration application and legal reachability of configuration-triggered first current-term commit.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Formal observation and source-based cycle correspondence answer the selected responsibility without converting elapsed time or process success into a verdict.',question_updates={cid:dict(unknowns=[],resume_conditions=[])}))\njson.dump(review,open('submission_review.json